   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 54 of the laws of 2016, directing the commissioner of education on how to recover certain penalties, in relation to the collection of a penalty from the Newburgh city school district",
    "basePrintNo": "S6404",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6404-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd Part A §49, Chap 54 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6404A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 54 of the laws of 2016, directing the\ncommissioner of education on how to recover certain penalties, in\nrelation to the collection of a penalty from the Newburgh city school\ndistrict\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo direct the commissioner of education to recover certain late final\ncost report penalties from the Newburgh city school district over a\n10-year recovery period beginning June 2018.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends section 49 of part A of chapter 54 of the laws of\n2016, directing the commissioner of education on to recover certain\nlate final cost report penalties from the Newburgh city school\ndistrict in 10 equal annual installments beginning June 2018.\n\nSection 2: Effective Date.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nUnder current law, the commissioner of education is directed to\nrecover certain late final cost report penalties over a 5-year period\nbeginning June 2017.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe 2017-18 state budget included provisions that provide certain\nschool districts facing penalties arising from untimely final cost\nreport filing with an optional 10-year stretch out period to pay the\npenalty. While the Newburgh Enlarged City School District's $12.7\nmillion final cost report penalty more than meets the law's intended\npurpose, the district was inadvertently left out under the adopted\nbudget language. This legislation would afford Newburgh similar\ntreatment and allow the school district to repay this penalty over a\nten year period beginning in June 2018.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
